<p>Thanks!</p>
<p>I hadn't heard of H.M. (thanks for bringing him to my attention, interesting!) but I was thinking of &quot;weaponised dementia&quot; later in the writing. These guys have a number of advantages over baseline humans but the Foundation finds a way to use their biggest weakness as a strength.</p>
<p>The before section was supposed to hint that the writer had memory issues, probably caused by the early stages of dementia. I may have been too subtle there. The pause before his secretary answers is because he's using the name of the person before her by mistake.</p>
<p>The not Daeva line was a very late addition. Before that I got some complaints about that bit and people just weren't getting it. Probably my fault. If I just dropped the &quot;not Daeva&quot; line and kept the &quot;non-Daeva occupation&quot; and &quot;style distinctly different to that typical of Daeva artifacts&quot; lines do you think it would work better?</p>
<p>I only found out about the D-class contest yesterday, just before I posted. I wrote this a while before that. Honestly, I don't think it fits the remit.</p>

